Reinterpreting Solution 2
We can think of this as the average in even more woman-centric terms. It’s the average difference between each woman applicant’s acceptance status, \(\textcolor[RGB]{0,191,196}{Y_i}\), and the mean acceptance status (i.e. rate) among men who applied to the same department, \(\textcolor[RGB]{248,118,109}{\hat \mu(0, X_i)}\).
\[
\color{gray}
\begin{aligned}
\text{summary}
&= \textcolor[RGB]{0,191,196}{\frac{1}{N_1}\sum_{i: W_i=1}} \left\{ * \right\}{ \textcolor[RGB]{0,191,196}{\hat \mu(1,X_i)} - \textcolor[RGB]{248,118,109}{\hat \mu(0, X_i)} }  
